{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:04:07.304930Z","id":"b0a721286c134613beb53c88c3034fcbcfe9c26f97ceded49be370ec3baa294a","body":{"detail":"Failure: any Debug or Profile macOS build with apps/clax_app/build-native/macos/clax present (`flutter build macos --debug`, `flutter test integration_test -d macos`, the desktop build that runs ClaudeCliBackend): Contents/Resources/clax is signed with macos/Runner/ClaxHelper.entitlements (com.apple.security.app-sandbox + com.apple.security.inherit) while the Runner is signed with macos/Runner/DebugProfile.entitlements, which has no app-sandbox (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md §3.2 and §12 D-5). A process carrying `inherit` whose parent is not sandboxed is killed at exec. Evidence: after `flutter build macos --debug`, `codesign -d --entitlements - build/macos/Build/Products/Debug/clax_app.app/Contents/Resources/clax` shows app-sandbox and inherit, and running that file exits 133 (SIGTRAP) with no output; the same debug clax unsigned prints `clax 0.4.0` and exits 0, and a scratch copy signed with `codesign --sign - --entitlements macos/Runner/ClaxHelper.entitlements --options runtime` also exits 133. So the supervisor's child never starts on the macOS Debug build. Spec §3.2 states the same unconditional signing, so the fix belongs in both places.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":343},"end":{"line":361},"content_hash":"27bd6873f34f8c912d2601469e96b6b3a4b04c4d492fd7f83ceab5296fa015f5"},"suggested_fix":"Choose the helper's entitlements by configuration: sign with ClaxHelper.entitlements only for Release (where Release.entitlements sandboxes the Runner), and for Debug/Profile sign with no entitlements (or a helper file without app-sandbox and inherit), e.g. `case \"$CONFIGURATION\" in Release) ent=\"$SRCROOT/Runner/ClaxHelper.entitlements\";; *) ent=\"\";; esac`. Then check that `Contents/Resources/clax --version` runs in both configurations.","summary":"The macOS Debug app's embedded clax traps at launch: the Embed clax phase signs it app-sandbox + inherit, but the Debug Runner is not sandboxed","tags":["review","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:07:37.346236Z","id":"ea22331f8fc804a9b9fa2c7fe567627f4b53952cb6857ef6afa5877608e452eb","body":{"detail":"After `flutter build macos --debug`: `build/macos/Build/Products/Debug/clax_app.app/Contents/Resources/clax --version` prints `clax 0.4.0` and exits 0; `codesign -d --entitlements -` on it lists no entitlements (flags adhoc,runtime). A Release build (xcodebuild -configuration Release, with CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS overridden to Release.entitlements minus keychain-access-groups, which needs a development certificate, see 467f9c1a): the helper's entitlements are app-sandbox and inherit, the app's are app-sandbox, audio-input, network.client and network.server, and `codesign --verify --deep --strict` passes. Run on its own the Release helper exits 133, as a sandbox-inheriting helper does without a sandboxed parent; running it under the app awaits the daemon supervisor.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The Embed clax phase signs with ClaxHelper.entitlements only when CONFIGURATION is Release; Debug and Profile sign without entitlements","supersedes":"b0a721286c134613beb53c88c3034fcbcfe9c26f97ceded49be370ec3baa294a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
